  "original_source_modified": false,
  "tensor_side_convention": "M tensor_A R is a right A-module tensor. Right modules are encoded as A-opposite modules. For commutative A, the printed tensor is explicitly identified with Mathlib TensorProduct. For general A, the full balanced quotient and its unique-lift property are proved.",
  "residual_augmentation_scope": "Original Claim 5.3 was completed in v0.11 for arbitrary finite p-groups in characteristic p, including nonabelian groups. The earlier abelian proof and its historical amendment remain preserved; the amendment is no longer active.",
  "artin_input_scope": "External Fact 8.1 supplies the canonical R-algebra equivalence R to the product of its actual localizations. This is an explicit theorem parameter, not a new Lean axiom. Its existence remains external; every module decomposition, localization comparison, and simultaneous generalized-eigenspace conclusion is proved.",
  "realization_input_scope": "Chebotarev conjugacy-saturated density, existence of a semisimplification representative preserving characteristic polynomials, the universal algebraic Brauer\u2013Nesbitt theorem, and the declared classicality/attached-polynomial input remain explicit supplied inputs. No conclusion-specific isomorphism is assumed, no new Lean axiom is introduced, and no external standard fact is promoted.",
  "external_realization_source_audit": "development/realization_scope_audit.md",
  "adequacy_definition_scope": "External Fact 4.1 supplies the terminology and adequacy convention, matched to Thorne, arXiv:1107.5989v1, Section 2, Definition 2.3. The ambient hypotheses are absolute irreducibility over a finite field containing all group-element eigenvalues. The four clauses are H0(ad0)=0, H1(k)=0, H1(ad0)=0, and generalized-eigenspace projector trace detection for every irreducible adjoint submodule. No adequacy theorem is assumed as a proof input. The external definition remains external and is not promoted into the internal-claim census.",
  "external_adequacy_source_audit": "development/adequacy_scope_audit.md",
  "independent_adequacy_review": "development/adequacy_independent_review.json",
