  "derived_definition_scope": {
    "6.14": "Derived support is the set of primes at which the actual residue-field derived fiber is not a zero object. Bounded finite-projective models compute this fiber, and independence under actual derived isomorphism is proved. ModuleCat scalar extension uses S tensor_R P, canonically the displayed P tensor_R^L S over a commutative ring. The definition remains a definition and is not added to the internal-claim census.",
    "6.17": "The datum uses a Noetherian patched ring, an actual ideal quotient ring identification, perfect models and an actual isomorphism in the derived category. The supplied comparison is the one required by the definition; neither fiber comparison nor invariance under derived isomorphism is an extra premise. The definition remains outside the internal-claim census."
  },
  "derived_external_fact_scope": {
    "6.15": "External Fact 6.15 remains an external standard fact in the original manuscript census. The needed zero-object criterion and faithful field-extension statement are proved using actual Mathlib complexes, cohomology and derived localization. No external theorem is added as a Lean axiom or unproved premise, and the external record is not promoted into the internal-claim census."
  },
